{
 "id": "inplace/deleted-by-a-later-change/cold-hot/5m",
 "description": "A pruner deletes nb, the last tool, which holds the client's cache mark. On request 1 it moves the mark onto bash, the last survivor: an in-place change of +10 tokens, reported once. On request 2 the pruner deletes bash too and moves the mark onto read. The bash mark move is not reported again, and the forwarded body has no item for it. The deletion of bash read the client's own 800 tokens, so it did not delete the mark move's output. The library must end the bash mark move (accountant#108). Request 2 prices the two deletions (1,400 tokens written) and the new mark move (10 tokens), and no check fails. Request 3 repeats the prune on a warm cache. Before the fix the bash mark move stayed active, and the sum and conservation checks failed on request 2 and every later request. The case models only the bytes of the mark, not a breakpoint on a tool, because the end rule does not read breakpoints.",
 "source": "issue_cases.md#108",
 "dims": {
  "kind": "rewrite",
  "position": "tools",
  "cache": "miss-hit",
